WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:03.920
What happens when you put a paper&nbsp;
origami swan into the Clockworks?

00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:09.120
Dr. Joe selected three white paper&nbsp;
origami swans, each weighing 29 grams.

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:14.320
The first paper swan was placed into SCP-914 on&nbsp;
the setting, "Rough." The output produced was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:19.520
one crumpled piece of white paper, weighing 29&nbsp;
grams. The second paper swan was placed on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.520 --> 00:00:24.480
setting "1:1," and the Clockworks produced&nbsp;
one paper "fortune teller" resembling those&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:29.600
popular with children. It had no writing on it.
The final paper swan was placed on the setting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:35.120
"Fine." The output was one paper model of a&nbsp;
trumpeter swan, the same size and weight as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.120 --> 00:00:40.320
the original origami. This paper model was&nbsp;
anatomically correct in every way, down to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:46.400
the impossibly intricate details of its internal&nbsp;
organs. There were no other anomalous properties.

